# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Health and readiness probes.
# WHEN:  First thing after `docker compose up` or `dotnet run`, before any
#        other request; also what Azure/monitoring will poll in production.
# WHY:   /health/live proves the process runs; /health/ready additionally
#        proves the database connection and applied migrations.
# WHERE: Sent to the API host selected via the Rider environment dropdown
#        (local-docker, local-dotnet, staging, production).
# AUTH:  None.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Liveness: process is up (200 even when the database is down)
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness: database reachable and schema ready (503 while db is starting)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Swagger UI (open in browser) - the admin interface of the MVP
# Development only; not exposed in production.
GET {{host}}/swagger/index.html

### OpenAPI document - use to diff the contract after API changes
GET {{host}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
